# Gradle
.gradle/
build/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# A second Gradle user home, made inside the project rather than beside it.
#
# A confined environment can only write under the project, and a Gradle that
# cannot write its own home cannot start at all: the wrapper's lock file lives in
# GRADLE_USER_HOME, which the instructions put outside this directory. Running the
# unpacked distribution with `-g .gradle-home` builds without that permission, at
# the cost of downloading the dependencies a second time. Kept so the next build is
# incremental; safe to delete whole, and never committed.
.gradle-home/
# The same arrangement for ANDROID_USER_HOME, which AGP also writes to. Holds the
# debug keystore this project's own debug builds are signed with.
.android-home/

# Android Studio / IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

# Kotlin compiler session data
.kotlin/

# Local machine configuration — never commit.
local.properties
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Local AI-agent instructions, not part of the published project.
AGENTS.md

# Local toolchain, kept beside the project instead of installed system-wide.
# .tools/git/ is a full portable Git (~390 MB); 签名密钥文件/ holds the real
# release keystore. The icon generator in .tools/图标生成/ is deliberately NOT
# ignored, because the README documents it as part of the project.
.tools/git/
.tools/签名密钥文件/
.tools/apk输出目录/
.tools/组件图片/
# Bug reports: screenshots and screen recordings of what went wrong on a device.
# Local evidence, not part of the project — the images the READMEs show live in docs/.
.tools/问题/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Build outputs
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
